t a  minute is this a good idea  I mean what when does this happen so  well so Nixon declares war on drugs he  pushes through the no-knock raid bill  through Congress and what happens a  couple things happens that so Congress  passed two bills one that applied to  federal narcotics agents doing federal  investigations anywhere in the country  the other bill applied only to the DC  Police Department because Congress has  jurisdiction over DC so what was  fascinating is there two different  reactions in DC the police chief at the  time Jerry Wilson was a very kind of  forward-thinking police chief took a  very less reactionary approach to crime  and he actually refused to implement the  no no no NOC law he said it wasn't  necessary he said you know there was no  need to barge in  people's homes like this and you know  oddly enough crime actually went down in  DC over the next few years while it went  up in the rest of the country at the  federal level things are very different  you had these narcotics agents who made  full use of this law and they were you  know raiding homes left and right they  were raiding homes without warrants they  were you know terrorizing innocent  people but these weren't SWAT teams  these were narcotics cops and street  clothes basically undercover cops and  they were kicking down doors and what  happened was there were a few raids that  really started to pick up some national  attention and Congress actually so it  shows some remorse and shame they they  hold hearings they bring victims in to  testify and they actually end up  repealing both no-knock laws and not  only that they pass another law making  the federal government liable any time a  federal agent commits the raid on the  wrong house so it was this rare moment  where you know the drug war was still  sort of intractable or wasn't completely  intractable Congress could actually  admitted made a mistake and gone a  little bit too far and actually rein  things in a little bit that's 